## Write the probability as a fraction
$P = \dfrac{\text{number who own both}}{\text{number surveyed}}$
P &= \frac{64}{168}
## Simplify the fraction
Divide the top and bottom by 8.
&= \frac{8}{21}
ANSWER: \frac{8}{21}

## Complete the tree diagram
Under Stalls (S), add Monday, Wednesday and Friday. At the end of every day, add V (VIP) and O (show only). This gives $2 \times 3 \times 2 = 12$ equally likely outcomes.
## Find the probability of Balcony, Wednesday, VIP
All choices are equally likely, so Balcony is $\frac12$, Wednesday is $\frac13$ and VIP is $\frac12$. Multiply along the branches.
P(BWV) &= \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2}
&= \frac{1}{12}
## Find the probability of Stalls, Wednesday, VIP
P(SWV) &= \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2}
&= \frac{1}{12}
## Add the two ways to get a VIP ticket on Wednesday
P(\text{VIP on Wednesday}) &= \frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{12}
&= \frac{2}{12}
&= \frac{1}{6}
ANSWER: \frac{1}{6}

